  "finding": "Class separation and novelty detection trade off. The metric objectives spread the known classes apart, which helps closed-set accuracy and covers more of the embedding sphere; an unknown flow is then more likely to land near some prototype. The least separated embedding rejects unknowns best. Small n -- 5 variants -- so this is a mechanism consistent with the data, not an established law.",
